                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1911-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="1911-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="1911-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>Roswell Pro Audio Delphos II</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Delphos II was introduced in 2019, replacing the Delphos in Roswell&#8217;s product line. The new version adds a 3rd polar pattern (Fig-8), a larger body (60mm diameter), and upgraded electronics.</p><p>Both models use a selected K67 style capsule with Roswell&#8217;s proprietary &#8220;K87&#8221; tuning. This capsule has a lower amplitude high-frequency presence peak than do most K67 capsules. Because the capsule needs less corrective EQ in the circuit, the mic&#8217;s high-frequency rolloff above 12kHz is more gradual than in mics whose capsules require more-aggressive correction, e.g. the Neumann U87. </p><p>The Delphos II retains the neutral tone, high sensitivity, and low distortion of the original. </p><p>The entire DC circuit, which generates polarization voltage for the capsule, was redesigned to eliminate inductors. This reduces the DC circuit&#8217;s ultrasonic noise. The new CMOS based DC converter is described as an &#8220;ultra low noise&#8221; design. It contains significant noise filtering, using high-cost capacitors that were selected in a blind listening test.</p><p>Numerous components in the audio circuit were upgraded in this redesign. All the electrolytic capacitors are Roswell&#8217;s bespoke formulation, which has a proprietary electrolyte gel and deep foil etching. Signal capacitors are European made, axial polypropylene types, designed specifically for audio. </p><p>The mic ships with the Roswell Cutaway&trade; shockmount, in a new ATA style hard case.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Roswell/Delphos-II">Roswell Pro Audio Delphos-II</a></p>
